  "analysis": "The Excel file seems to have a header or title row that messed up the default reading, as indicated by 'Unnamed' columns and mostly NaN values. The shape (47, 9) is also suspicious for a 'large-scale' file, suggesting I might be looking at a title sheet or the wrong sheet entirely. I need to check all sheet names to find the actual data.",
  "plan": "1. Update `inspect_data.py` to list all sheet names in the Excel file.
2. Read and print the head of all sheets to identify which one contains the game data.
3. Execute the updated script.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat <<EOF > inspect_data.py
